    "r3Location": "products/rea-studio/apps/notes/client.mjs:128-131",
    "finding": "After an actual first save committed and accept(note) took ownership, a delayed list/notebook refresh error was checked only against editor generation. Newer ordinary typing in that same editor changed the draft revision without changing generation. The stale error could overwrite the newer unsaved-draft status and obscure the fact that the save had committed.",
    "r4Correction": "The save request and post-commit refresh now have distinct catches. Error and final-success publication require mounted state, matching generation, draft revision and all four current field values; post-commit refresh failure explicitly preserves the committed save result.",
    "addedRegression": "One source UI group first requires truthful committed-save/refresh-error wording, then holds an actual post-accept list reply, types a newer body, rejects that reply, preserves body/status and saves again with the committed ID/revision without newTodo.",
